# Artifacts directory

For plans, analyses, reviews, and other generated artifacts—and whenever the user says **"the artifacts directory"** (or similar: "artifact path", "save to artifacts", "write the analysis md"):

1. Use the **relevant subdirectory** under **`$AGENT_ARTIFACTS_HOME`**, not a repository-local artifact directory unless they explicitly ask for that.
2. Default home: exported **`AGENT_ARTIFACTS_HOME`**, else **`~/Documents/agent-artifacts`**.
3. General technical-analysis reference belongs under **`$AGENT_ARTIFACTS_HOME/knowledge/`** (`$KNOWLEDGE/`) — store root, **not** under **`<repo-key>/`**.
4. Cross-repo org knowledge belongs under **`$AGENT_ARTIFACTS_HOME/_global/`** (`$GLOBAL/`).

## Path shape

```text
$AGENT_ARTIFACTS_HOME/knowledge/
$AGENT_ARTIFACTS_HOME/<repo-key>/<meaningful_id>/
$AGENT_ARTIFACTS_HOME/_global/<topic>/
```

- **`<repo-key>`** — from `git remote get-url origin` (e.g. `github.com-snyk-cli`), or sanitized repo folder name.
- **`<meaningful_id>`** — from context: Jira key (`CLI-1474`), PR/MR id (`pr-336`, `mr-1447`), branch/topic slug, etc.

## Examples

| Context | Path |
|---------|------|
| CLI-1474 on snyk/cli | `$AGENT_ARTIFACTS_HOME/github.com-snyk-cli/CLI-1474/` |
| MR 1447 on snyk/cli | `$AGENT_ARTIFACTS_HOME/github.com-snyk-cli/mr-1447/` |
| General knowledge (technical-analysis) | `$AGENT_ARTIFACTS_HOME/knowledge/` |
| Cross-repo org notes | `$AGENT_ARTIFACTS_HOME/_global/` |

## Resolution

When the repo or id is unclear, run (Cursor skills root shown; Codex uses `~/.codex/skills/scripts/`):

```bash
python3 ~/.cursor/skills/scripts/resolve_artifact_path.py --repo-artifacts-root
python3 ~/.cursor/skills/scripts/resolve_artifact_path.py --meaningful-id <ID> --basename <file>.md
python3 ~/.cursor/skills/scripts/resolve_artifact_path.py --knowledge-artifacts-root
python3 ~/.cursor/skills/scripts/resolve_artifact_path.py --scope knowledge --basename <file>.md
python3 ~/.cursor/skills/scripts/resolve_artifact_path.py --global-artifacts-root
python3 ~/.cursor/skills/scripts/resolve_artifact_path.py --scope global \
  --meaningful-id <topic> --basename <file>.md
```

Read existing files in the target directory before creating duplicates. Prefer extending an existing analysis/review artifact in place.

Schema: **`~/.cursor/skills/ARTIFACTS.md`** (or **`~/.codex/skills/ARTIFACTS.md`** on Codex).
